        "rationale": "The initial unresolved distinction is whether early progress is primarily limited by physical control authority and sampled-data settling or by learned policy behavior. This candidate-free measurement directly tests the model assumptions about compiler-derived dynamics, joint limits, self-contact, and braking. If responses settle rapidly with adequate authority and branches are collision-free, the next direction should prioritize policy learning and hold diagnostics; if settling is slow, saturated, asymmetric, or branch contacts occur, the first learning design should explicitly account for stabilization, action bandwidth, or branch selection."
